#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1307
msgid ""
"The minimum distance between the slider and viewport edges when Performance "
"Mode should activate as described on the right. Supported units: <br><br> "
"<b>px:</b> A fixed value specified in pixels. <br><br> <b>%</b> or <b>sh:</"
"b> Percentage of the slider height. 1sh equals to 1% of the slider height. "
"This value scales dynamically when the slider’s size changes. <b> <br><br> "
"vh:</b> Percentage of the viewport (browser window) height. 1vh equals to 1% "
"of the viewport height. This value scales dynamically when the browser "
"window is resized."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1313
msgid ""
"The scene position to animate to. Supported units: <br><br> <b>%:</b> "
"Percentage of the scene’s length. 0% means the beginning, while 100% means "
"the end of the scene. <br><br> <b>ms:</b> A specific point in time on the "
"scene’s animation timeline in milliseconds. A second is 1000 milliseconds. "
"Sticky scenes do not support this unit."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1317
msgid ""
"The position within the target scene to scroll to. Leave it empty to scroll "
"to the beginning of the scene. Supported units: <br><br> <b>%:</b> "
"Percentage of the scene’s length. 0% means the beginning, while 100% means "
"the end of the scene. <br><br> <b>ms:</b> A specific point in time on the "
"scene’s animation timeline in milliseconds. A second is 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1321
msgid ""
"The timeline position to animate to or the amount to play forward/backward. "
"Supported units: <br><br> <b>%:</b> Percentage of the slide duration. 0% "
"means the beginning, while 100% means the end of the slide timeline. "
"<br><br> <b>ms:</b> A specific point or amount of time in milliseconds. A "
"second is 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1326
msgid ""
"Adjusts the width of the border in pixels. Larger values create a thicker, "
"more prominent border."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1330
msgid ""
"Specifies whether the border is drawn inside or outside the layer’s edges."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1334
msgid ""
"Adjusts the distance between the border and the layer’s edges. You can use "
"positive and negative values."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1338
msgid ""
"Determines whether the border animation plays sequentially around the "
"selected sides or all at once."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1342
msgid "Controls the border animation’s movement."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1346
msgid ""
"Sets how long the border animation takes from beginning to end in "
"milliseconds. A second equals to 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1347
msgid ""
"In Sequential mode, this time is divided among the selected sides, so each "
"side animates more quickly to fit within the overall length."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1351
msgid ""
"Sets how long to wait before the border animation begins, in milliseconds, "
"relative to the selected <b>START AT</b> option. A second equals to 1000 "
"milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1355
msgid "Specifies which axes can be deformed when reacting to pointer movement."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1359
msgid ""
"Adjusts the maximum horizontal stretching applied to the layer while "
"following the pointer. Larger values create more pronounced deformation."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1363
msgid ""
"Adjusts the maximum vertical stretching applied to the layer. Leave this "
"field empty to automatically calculate a proportional value based on the X "
"setting and the layer’s dimensions."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1367
msgid ""
"Sets how much the layer can skew as it reacts to pointer movement. Higher "
"values create a more noticeable distortion."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1371
msgid ""
"Controls the maximum rotation applied during deformation. Larger values "
"allow the layer to tilt more while following the pointer."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1375
msgid ""
"Determines how strongly the layer reacts to pointer movement. Higher values "
"make the layer reach its maximum deformation more quickly, requiring smaller "
"pointer movements to achieve the full effect."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1379
msgid ""
"Sets how long it takes for the layer to reach its deformed state while "
"following the pointer, measured in milliseconds. One second equals 1000 "
"milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1383
msgid ""
"Sets how long it takes for the layer to return to its original shape after "
"the pointer leaves the layer, measured in milliseconds. One second equals "
"1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1387
msgid ""
"Determines how the layer behaves when moving back to its original position "
"after the pointer leaves the layer. <ul><li><b>Tethered:</b> Returns without "
"noticeable overshoot.<br><br></li><li><b>Natural:</b> Adds a small amount of "
"overshoot for a subtle, smoother feel.<br><br></li><li><b>Bouncy:</b> "
"Applies a stronger overshoot, creating a more pronounced spring-like motion."
"</li></ul>"
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1391
msgid "Sets the number of copies to generate from the original layer."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1395
msgid ""
"Delays each copy’s animation by a set number of milliseconds. This delay is "
"added on top of the previous one, so it accumulates for each additional "
"copy. One second equals 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1399
#, no-php-format
msgid ""
"Shifts each copy’s position horizontally by the specified amount, as if they "
"were created at an offset location from the original. The shift is "
"cumulative when using fixed values, so each copy is placed further from the "
"previous one. When using randomized values or expressions, however, each "
"copy is calculated independently and the shift is not cumulative. You can "
"use positive and negative values. Randomized values are also supported, but "
"avoid mixing units. Supported units: <ul><li><b>px:</b> A fixed value "
"specified in pixels.<br><br></li><li><b>sw:</b> Percentage of the slider "
"width. 1sw equals to 1% of the slider width. This value scales dynamically "
"when the slider’s size changes.<br><br></li><li><b>lw:</b> Percentage of the "
"layer width. 1lw equals to 1% of the layer width. This value scales "
"dynamically when the layer’s size changes.</li></ul>"
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1403
#, no-php-format
msgid ""
"Shifts each copy’s position vertically by the specified amount, as if they "
"were created at an offset location from the original. The shift is "
"cumulative when using fixed values, so each copy is placed further from the "
"previous one. When using randomized values or expressions, however, each "
"copy is calculated independently and the shift is not cumulative. You can "
"use positive and negative values. Randomized values are also supported, but "
"avoid mixing units. Supported units: <ul><li><b>px:</b> A fixed value "
"specified in pixels.<br><br></li><li><b>sh:</b> Percentage of the slider "
"height. 1sh equals to 1% of the slider height. This value scales dynamically "
"when the slider’s size changes.<br><br></li><li><b>lh:</b> Percentage of the "
"layer height. 1lh equals to 1% of the layer height. This value scales "
"dynamically when the layer’s size changes.</li></ul>"
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1407
msgid ""
"Defines the lower limit of the opacity applied across copies. By default, "
"copies gradually fade between the Max and Min values, and the distribution "
"is controlled by the Fade Method setting."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1411
msgid ""
"Defines the upper limit of the opacity applied across copies. By default, "
"copies gradually fade between the Max and Min values, and the distribution "
"is controlled by the Fade Method setting."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1415
msgid ""
"Determines how opacity values are distributed between the Max and Min "
"settings across copies. Different methods use various curves to define the "
"progression, creating either even or non-linear value sequences."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1419
msgid ""
"Adjusts the scale transformation for each additional copy by the specified "
"step value. Positive values progressively enlarge copies, while negative "
"values shrink them. When using random values, each copy will receive a "
"randomly chosen value from the defined range. When using cycle values, "
"copies will take the defined values in order, one after another."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1423
msgid ""
"Adjusts the rotation for each additional copy by the specified step value. "
"Positive values progressively rotate copies clockwise, while negative values "
"rotate them counterclockwise. When using random values, each copy will "
"receive a randomly chosen value from the defined range. When using cycle "
"values, copies will take the defined values in order, one after another."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1427
msgid ""
"Adjusts the width of each additional copy by the specified step value. "
"Positive values progressively increase the width, while negative values "
"decrease it."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1431
msgid ""
"Adjusts the height of each additional copy by the specified step value. "
"Positive values progressively increase the height, while negative values "
"decrease it."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1435
msgid ""
"Adjusts the parallax level of the Parallax Transition for each additional "
"copy by the specified step value. Positive values progressively increase the "
"parallax effect, while negative values decrease it."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1439
msgid ""
"Adjusts the movement duration of the Parallax Transition for each additional "
"copy by the specified step value. Positive values progressively increase the "
"duration, while negative values shorten it."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1443
msgid ""
"Sets how long to wait before the typing animation begins, in milliseconds, "
"relative to the selected <b>START AT</b> option. A second equals to 1000 "
"milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1447
msgid ""
"Sets the delay before the cursor gets hidden after the animation finishes, "
"in milliseconds. This only applies when Hide After Animation is enabled. A "
"second equals 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1451
msgid ""
"Sets the time for the mask to expand and fully cover the layer, in "
"milliseconds. A second equals 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1455
msgid ""
"Sets how long the mask stays fully covering the layer before collapsing, in "
"milliseconds. A second equals 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1459
msgid ""
"Sets the time for the mask to collapse and reveal the layer’s content, in "
"milliseconds. A second equals 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1463
msgid ""
"Sets the time offset between individual tiles when the selected animation "
"consists of multiple segments. This delay is cumulative, so each subsequent "
"tile starts later than the previous one by the specified amount. Measured in "
"milliseconds, where one second equals 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1467
msgid ""
"Sets how many slices the layer is cut into. Fewer slices create bold, chunky "
"fragments, while more slices produce a finer, smoother scattering. You can "
"use up to 20 slices."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1471
msgid ""
"Determines how the layer is cut and which way the slices travel. Diagonal "
"options produce angled cuts, while Vertical and Horizontal split the layer "
"into straight columns or rows."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1475
msgid ""
"Controls how far each slice travels from its original position, measured in "
"pixels. Larger values create a more dramatic, widely scattered result. "
"Neighboring slices move in opposite directions, so the layer pulls itself "
"apart. Randomized values are also supported, in which case every slice "
"receives its own value from the defined range."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1479
msgid ""
"Sets the scale each slice grows or shrinks to while it travels. Values above "
"1 make slices end up enlarged, while values below 1 make them end up "
"smaller. Randomized values are also supported, in which case every slice "
"receives its own value from the defined range."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1483
msgid ""
"Adds spacing between the slices in pixels, trimming each slice along its "
"edges. This creates a visible seam between the fragments as they pull apart."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1487
msgid ""
"Sets how long each slice takes to travel to its scattered position, in "
"milliseconds. A second equals to 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: assets/templates/tmpl-smart-help.php:1491
msgid ""
"Shifts when the slicing animation begins, relative to the Start At option, "
"in milliseconds. Use 0 to start exactly there, or negative values to start "
"earlier so the animations overlap. A second equals to 1000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

